 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "title-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Wikipedia2Vec Hidden-Connection Finder — Google Colab Quick-Start\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook runs the **Wikipedia2Vec temporal knowledge-gap experiment** entirely in the cloud.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pipeline:**\n",
    "1. Install dependencies & clone the repo\n",
    "2. *(Optional)* Mount Google Drive to persist large files between sessions\n",
    "3. Download pre-trained embeddings + Wikipedia pagelinks dump\n",
    "4. Parse the link graph\n",
    "5. Find hidden connections (high-similarity, unlinked entity pairs)\n",
    "6. *(Optional)* Validate predictions against a later dump\n",
    "\n",
    "**Runtime estimates (free Colab, 20 k entities):**\n",
    "| Step | Time |\n",
    "|------|------|\n",
    "| Install & clone | ~1 min |\n",
    "| Download model (~1.4 GB) | ~3–8 min |\n",
    "| Download pagelinks dump (~2–5 GB) | ~10–20 min |\n",
    "| Parse link graph | ~10–30 min |\n",
    "| Find hidden connections | ~5–15 min |\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Tip:** Mount Google Drive (Step 2) so large downloads survive session restarts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "step1-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Install dependencies & clone the repo"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "install-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install Python packages\n",
    "!pip install -q wikipedia2vec numpy scipy scikit-learn pandas matplotlib tqdm networkx\n",
    "\n",
    "# Clone the experiment repository\n",
    "import os\n",
    "REPO_DIR = \"/content/ClaudeExperiment\"\n",
    "if not os.path.isdir(REPO_DIR):\n",
    "    !git clone https://github.com/sumit7194/ClaudeExperiment.git \"$REPO_DIR\"\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Repo already present, pulling latest...\")\n",
    "    !git -C \"$REPO_DIR\" pull\n",
    "\n",
    "%cd \"$REPO_DIR\"\n",
    "print(\"Working directory:\", os.getcwd())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "step2-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 — (Optional) Mount Google Drive for persistent storage\n",
    "\n",
    "Large files (model ~1.4 GB, pagelinks dumps ~2–5 GB each) survive Colab session restarts\n",
    "when stored on Drive.  \n",
    "**Skip this step** if you prefer to re-download every session."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "drive-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "USE_DRIVE = True  # Set to False to use ephemeral /content storage\n",
    "\n",
    "if USE_DRIVE:\n",
    "    from google.colab import drive\n",
    "    drive.mount(\"/content/drive\")\n",
    "    DATA_DIR = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/wikipedia2vec_data\"\n",
    "    RESULTS_DIR = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/wikipedia2vec_results\"\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    DATA_DIR = \"/content/ClaudeExperiment/data\"\n",
    "    RESULTS_DIR = \"/content/ClaudeExperiment/results\"\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "os.makedirs(DATA_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs(RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "print(f\"Data dir   : {DATA_DIR}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Results dir: {RESULTS_DIR}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "step3-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 — Download pre-trained Wikipedia2Vec model\n",
    "\n",
    "We use the **English 300-dimensional model** trained on the April 2018 Wikipedia dump (~1.4 GB compressed).  \n",
    "Source: [wikipedia2vec.github.io/wikipedia2vec/pretrained](https://wikipedia2vec.github.io/wikipedia2vec/pretrained/)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "download-model-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "BASE_DATE = \"20180420\"\n",
    "MODEL_FILENAME = f\"enwiki_{BASE_DATE}_300d.pkl.bz2\"\n",
    "MODEL_PATH = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, MODEL_FILENAME)\n",
    "\n",
    "MODEL_URL = f\"http://wikipedia2vec.s3.amazonaws.com/models/en/2018-04-20/{MODEL_FILENAME}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.isfile(MODEL_PATH):\n",
    "    print(f\"Model already downloaded: {MODEL_PATH}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Downloading model (~1.4 GB) — this may take several minutes...\")\n",
    "    !wget -q --show-progress -O \"$MODEL_PATH\" \"$MODEL_URL\"\n",
    "    print(\"Download complete.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "step4-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 — Download Wikipedia pagelinks dump\n",
    "\n",
    "We need two files for the **base** date (April 2018):\n",
    "- `pagelinks.sql.gz` — the link graph (~2–5 GB)\n",
    "- `page.sql.gz` — maps page IDs to titles (~500 MB–1 GB)\n",
    "\n",
    "Source: [dumps.wikimedia.org/enwiki](https://dumps.wikimedia.org/enwiki/)\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Note:** Wikipedia dump archives are large. The download may take 10–20 minutes on free Colab."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "download-dumps-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Base date for the dump — must match the pre-trained model\n",
    "DUMP_MONTH = BASE_DATE[:6]  # e.g. \"201804\"\n",
    "\n",
    "PAGELINKS_FILENAME = f\"enwiki-{DUMP_MONTH}01-pagelinks.sql.gz\"\n",
    "PAGE_FILENAME      = f\"enwiki-{DUMP_MONTH}01-page.sql.gz\"\n",
    "\n",
    "PAGELINKS_PATH = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, PAGELINKS_FILENAME)\n",
    "PAGE_PATH      = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, PAGE_FILENAME)\n",
    "\n",
    "BASE_URL = f\"https://dumps.wikimedia.org/enwiki/{DUMP_MONTH}01\"\n",
    "\n",
    "for path, filename, desc in [\n",
    "    (PAGE_PATH,      PAGE_FILENAME,      \"page dump (~500 MB)\"),\n",
    "    (PAGELINKS_PATH, PAGELINKS_FILENAME, \"pagelinks dump (~2–5 GB)\"),\n",
    "]:\n",
    "    if os.path.isfile(path):\n",
    "        print(f\"Already downloaded: {path}\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        url = f\"{BASE_URL}/{filename}\"\n",
    "        print(f\"Downloading {desc}...\")\n",
    "        !wget -q --show-progress -O \"$path\" \"$url\"\n",
    "        print(f\"  Saved to {path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "step5-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5 — Parse the base link graph"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "parse-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "BASE_LINKS_PATH = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, f\"links_{BASE_DATE}.json\")\n",
    "SCRIPTS_DIR = os.path.join(REPO_DIR, \"scripts\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.isfile(BASE_LINKS_PATH):\n",
    "    print(f\"Link graph already parsed: {BASE_LINKS_PATH}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Parsing link graph — this may take 10–30 minutes...\")\n",
    "    !python \"$SCRIPTS_DIR/parse_pagelinks.py\" \\\n",
    "        --pagelinks \"$PAGELINKS_PATH\" \\\n",
    "        --page      \"$PAGE_PATH\" \\\n",
    "        --output    \"$BASE_LINKS_PATH\"\n",
    "    print(f\"Link graph saved to {BASE_LINKS_PATH}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "step6-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6 — Find hidden connections\n",
    "\n",
    "Scans the top `limit_entities` Wikipedia entities, computing cosine similarity between\n",
    "their embeddings. Pairs that are **similar but NOT linked** become "hidden connection" candidates."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "find-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "CANDIDATES_PATH = os.path.join(RESULTS_DIR, f\"candidates_{BASE_DATE}.json\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tune these to trade speed for coverage\n",
    "THRESHOLD      = 0.65   # minimum cosine similarity to flag as a candidate\n",
    "MAX_PAIRS      = 50000  # cap total candidates written\n",
    "LIMIT_ENTITIES = 20000  # only examine the top-N entities by frequency\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.isfile(CANDIDATES_PATH):\n",
    "    print(f\"Candidates already computed: {CANDIDATES_PATH}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Finding hidden connections — this may take 5–15 minutes...\")\n",
    "    !python \"$SCRIPTS_DIR/find_hidden_connections.py\" \\\n",
    "        --model           \"$MODEL_PATH\" \\\n",
    "        --links           \"$BASE_LINKS_PATH\" \\\n",
    "        --output          \"$CANDIDATES_PATH\" \\\n",
    "        --threshold       \"$THRESHOLD\" \\\n",
    "        --max-pairs       \"$MAX_PAIRS\" \\\n",
    "        --limit-entities  \"$LIMIT_ENTITIES\"\n",
    "    print(f\"Candidates saved to {CANDIDATES_PATH}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "step7-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7 — Inspect results"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "inspect-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "with open(CANDIDATES_PATH) as f:\n",
    "    candidates = json.load(f)\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(candidates)\n",
    "print(f\"Total candidates: {len(df):,}\")\n",
    "df.sort_values(\"similarity\", ascending=False).head(20)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "step8-header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 8 — (Optional) Validate against a later Wikipedia dump\n",
    "\n",
    "Download a more recent pagelinks + page dump, parse it, then run the validator to see\n",
    "how many predicted connections actually appeared in Wikipedia later."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "validate-download-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Change LATER_DATE to whichever dump you want to validate against.\n",
    "LATER_DATE  = \"20250101\"\n",
    "LATER_MONTH = LATER_DATE[:6]\n",
    "\n",
    "LATER_PAGELINKS_PATH = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, f\"enwiki-{LATER_MONTH}01-pagelinks.sql.gz\")\n",
    "LATER_PAGE_PATH      = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, f\"enwiki-{LATER_MONTH}01-page.sql.gz\")\n",
    "LATER_LINKS_PATH     = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, f\"links_{LATER_DATE}.json\")\n",
    "\n",
    "LATER_BASE_URL = f\"https://dumps.wikimedia.org/enwiki/{LATER_MONTH}01\"\n",
    "\n",
    "for path, filename, desc in [\n",
    "    (LATER_PAGE_PATH,      f\"enwiki-{LATER_MONTH}01-page.sql.gz\",      \"later page dump\"),\n",
    "    (LATER_PAGELINKS_PATH, f\"enwiki-{LATER_MONTH}01-pagelinks.sql.gz\", \"later pagelinks dump\"),\n",
    "]:\n",
    "    if os.path.isfile(path):\n",
    "        print(f\"Already downloaded: {path}\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        url = f\"{LATER_BASE_URL}/{filename}\"\n",
    "        print(f\"Downloading {desc}...\")\n",
    "        !wget -q --show-progress -O \"$path\" \"$url\"\n",
    "        print(f\"  Saved to {path}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "validate-parse-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if os.path.isfile(LATER_LINKS_PATH):\n",
    "    print(f\"Later link graph already parsed: {LATER_LINKS_PATH}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Parsing later link graph...\")\n",
    "    !python \"$SCRIPTS_DIR/parse_pagelinks.py\" \\\n",
    "        --pagelinks \"$LATER_PAGELINKS_PATH\" \\\n",
    "        --page      \"$LATER_PAGE_PATH\" \\\n",
    "        --output    \"$LATER_LINKS_PATH\"\n",
    "    print(f\"Saved to {LATER_LINKS_PATH}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "validate-run-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Running validation...\")\n",
    "!python \"$SCRIPTS_DIR/validate_predictions.py\" \\\n",
    "    --candidates  \"$CANDIDATES_PATH\" \\\n",
    "    --links-later \"$LATER_LINKS_PATH\" \\\n",
    "    --links-base  \"$BASE_LINKS_PATH\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "plot-cell",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Display the precision@K plot inline\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from IPython.display import Image, display\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_path = os.path.join(RESULTS_DIR, \"precision_at_k.png\")\n",
    "if os.path.isfile(plot_path):\n",
    "    display(Image(plot_path))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Plot not found — run the validation step first.\")"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
